== Behavior ==

From the blank tape, bounded simulation did not halt through <math>10^8</math> raw steps. The only undefined transition is state '''F''' reading '''0''', and F is entered only via <code>C0 = 0RF</code> — so the machine halts iff state C ever reads a 0 with a second 0 immediately to its right.

At tape-frontier records the machine locks (97.8% of transitions) into a frozen-prefix sweep over the rightmost three runs of ones:

: <math>(\ldots, a, b, c) \mapsto (\ldots, a+2,\, b-2,\, c+1)</math>

When the middle run is exhausted (reaches 1), the rightmost three runs merge:

: <math>(\ldots, a, 1, c) \mapsto (\ldots, a+c+4)</math>

and after a full collapse to a single run of <math>n</math> ones, the tape re-expands via <math>(n) \to (n,1) \to (1,n,1) \to (2,\,n-2,\,2)</math> and the sweep restarts.

=== Exact macro system ===

Over the augmented frontier-record state (machine state, frontier side, run-length tuple) — the run-length tuple alone is ''not'' deterministic — a fitted system of '''36 generalized rules''' (constant-delta and exact rational affine maps with guards) plus 7 startup literals reproduces the machine's record dynamics '''exactly''':

* in-sample: 3,832/3,832 record transitions (20M-step fit run), zero mismatches;
* out-of-sample: 4,150/4,150 record transitions beyond the fit horizon in a fresh 100M-step run, zero mismatches, zero uncovered.

=== Recursive checkpoint law ===

Full-collapse (single-run) checkpoint values observed in <math>10^8</math> steps:

: <math>1, 1, 5, 11, 20, 67, 104, 277, 419, 632, 2070, 5378</math>

Consecutive checkpoint pairs whose intervening dynamics stay within three runs satisfy exactly

: <math>n \text{ odd:}\quad n' = \frac{3n+7}{2}</math>

(verified 5/5: <math>5\to11,\ 11\to20,\ 67\to104,\ 277\to419,\ 419\to632</math>; no failures). Even checkpoint values never step directly: each spawns a hierarchical epoch in which a frozen prefix holds while the suffix runs the same sweep/merge dynamics one level down (runs of up to 5 blocks observed); the pairs <math>20\to67,\ 104\to277,\ 632\to2070,\ 2070\to5378</math> are compositions of these sub-epochs. "Odd steps simply, even recurses" distinguishes this machine from flat Collatz iterators such as [[Antihydra]].

== Halt localization ==

A census of every F-entry over <math>10^8</math> steps (7,947 events):

* F read '''1 every time''' (no halt);
* the local 9-cell window at C's probe takes only '''10 distinct shapes''', the dominant one (99.1%) being <code>1111·0·1111</code> — C probing a single-0 gap between two runs, immediately left of the rightmost run;
* aligning every F-entry with the macro rule firing in its record interval: 27 of 30 rules produce exactly one window shape, 3 boundary rules produce two, with zero unmatched intervals.

The candidate halt-unreachability invariant — ''every 0-gap that state C probes has length exactly 1'' — therefore reduces to '''33 (rule, window) local obligations''': for each pair, show that the rule's raw micro-trajectory only probes C-reads-0 in that window shape. Note the invariant is not "all gaps have length 1" (length-2 interior gaps do occur at records); it is a claim about which gaps C ''probes''.

All 33 obligations have been mechanically discharged at the empirical level (fail-closed): across every firing of every rule in <math>10^8</math> steps the C-probe sites are uniform relative to the block structure (counts constant or exactly affine in the variable block lengths), and synthetic replays on fresh, never-observed block values (59/59) reproduce both the macro prediction and the probe structure. This establishes the uniform-crossing premise the induction needs; it is not itself a proof.

== Why it may be a cryptid ==

The machine survives the local sound decider chain at expanded budget (bounded halt, exact/translated cycle, backward reasoning, sound bouncer, CTL, FAR/closed-set DFA). Its dynamics are low-dimensional and exactly characterized rather than featureless, and the halting condition reduces to a single non-regular local invariant of the "state X reads s" class — the same class as the known open BB(6) frontier, but here with an exactly verified macro system available to carry the induction.

